@startuml

title A metered page request

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #333333
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBorderColor #333333
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

actor "reader" as V
participant "site server" as S
participant "RPC" as R
participant "pay_on_chain" as P #pink
participant "SPL Token" as T #pink

== GET: never meters, never charges ==

V -> S : GET /a/{slug}
activate S

S -> S : session cookie -> meter and fund?

break no session
  S -> R : getMultipleAccounts(site, treasury, mint)
  R --> S : account data
  S -[#00A0A0]-> V : lede + meter panel (set_meter)
  note right of V
    Identifying happens here, on the
    article: a key proof if this browser
    holds a key and a meter, or the setup
    scan if it does not. There is no
    sign-in page; see SPEC section 5.
  end note
end

break live view grant for this article
  opt its charge is still pending
    S -> R : getSignatureStatuses (once, history search)
    R --> S : status
    S -> S : write what became of the charge onto the grant
  end
  S -> R : getMultipleAccounts(site, treasury, mint, meter, fund token account)
  R --> S : account data
  S -[#00A0A0]-> V : metered_page (no charge)
end

S -[#00A0A0]-> V : shell: lede + "checking your meter..."
note right of V
  No chain read on this response.
  The POST's answer fills the
  inspector; see SPEC section 9.
end note
deactivate S

== POST: the page view ==

V -> S : POST /a/{slug} (the shell's script at once; without one, a button)
activate S

S -> S : session -> meter, fund, key; derive the fund's token account
S -> R : getMultipleAccounts(site, treasury, mint, meter, fund token account)
R --> S : account data
S -> S : decode Site, Meter, TokenAccount

break no meter account (closed elsewhere)
  S -> S : end the session
  S -[#00A0A0]-> V : set_meter
end

break the meter names another key (renewed from another device)
  S -> S : end the session
  S -[#00A0A0]-> V : set_meter
end

group meter lock -- BEGIN IMMEDIATE on the meter's row (SPEC section 7.2)

  break grant is live (a repeated POST)
    S -[#00A0A0]-> V : metered_page (no charge)
  end

  S -> R : getMultipleAccounts(meter, fund token account)
  R --> S : account data
  note right of S
    Read again, inside the lock. A request
    that queued behind another decides from
    what that one left, not from what it
    saw before it waited.
  end note

  S -> S : preflight can_meter(meter, site, 1, now)
  break blocked: Expired or LimitReached
    S -[#00A0A0]-> V : manage_meter
  end

  S -> S : build meter_and_settle
  S -> R : getLatestBlockhash
  R --> S : blockhash
  S -> S : sign as site authority

  S -> R : sendTransaction
  R -> R : simulate against current state
  break the simulation fails
    R --> S : error, nothing sent
    S -> S : cause(first raising program, code); discard logs
    S -[#00A0A0]-> V : manage_meter, or "the fund is short": add to the fund
  end
  R --> S : signature
  S -> S : record view grant, charge pending; count the purchase
end

S -[#00A0A0]-> V : metered_page + inspector, no account figures (swapped into the shell)
note right of V
  Served before the chain answers.
  A read now would show the accounts
  from before the charge, so the strip
  says the charge is on its way instead.
end note
deactivate S

R -> P : meter_and_settle(items = 1)
  activate P
  P -> P : require now <= expiry
  P -> P : used += item_price
  P -> P : require used <= limit
  alt used - paid >= collection_threshold
    P -> T : transfer_checked(fund token account -> treasury), signed by the fund's seeds
    T --> P : ok
    P -> P : paid = used
  end
P --> R : Metered event
deactivate P

== POST confirm: afterward, charges nothing ==

V -> S : POST /a/{slug}/confirm (the page's script, at once)
activate S
S -> R : getSignatureStatuses (up to 6 asks, 2 s apart; history search)
R --> S : status
S -> S : write onto the grant: confirmed, refused, or still pending
note right of S
  The grant stays whatever the answer.
  A charge that landed and failed was
  already served: the site takes the loss
  (SPEC section 7.3).
end note
opt confirmed
  S -> R : getTransaction
  R --> S : Metered event (did it settle?)
end
S -> R : getMultipleAccounts(site, treasury, mint, meter, fund token account)
R --> S : account data
note right of S
  The charge moved used, paid and the
  fund's balance, so the page reads them
  again. Claim 7 in SPEC section 2: every
  number on the screen came from an
  account, not from the server's memory.
end note

S -[#00A0A0]-> V : metered_page + inspector (swapped in; the instruction rows are kept)
deactivate S

legend left
Colour follows state-machine.plantuml in the sol-pay repository.
  pink ..... on chain
  teal ..... a screen this site builds
Every break is a screen, not an error page.
A GET never meters: the charge is the POST (SPEC section 7.1).
The site authority signs meter_and_settle. The reader and the wallet are not present.
The session was bound by a key proof (SPEC section 5.3); each charge re-reads
the meter, so a renewal from another device ends this session at its next read.
The article is served before the charge confirms; see SPEC section 7.3.
endlegend

@enduml
